    "summary": "Dark Star/MLB fireworks and tight second‑set jams",
    "blurb": "The show erupts with a smoking Dark Star into a Mind Left Body jam, highlighted by Jerry’s crisp leads and Phil’s thunderous solo. Playing In The Band drives the second set with high‑octane drumming, and the encore lands an soaring Eyes Of The World followed by a soulful Stella Blue.",
    "review": "On October 19, 1973 at the Oklahoma City Fairgrounds Arena the Dead delivered one of those rare nights where the improvisational spark truly ignites. After a wobbly start – the early first‑set mix favoring keyboards over guitars – the band quickly finds its footing, building to an explosive Playing In The Band that showcases Bill Kreutzmann’s extra‑limb energy and Jerry Garcia’s on‑fire solo work. The second set is where the magic lives: a blistering Dark Star that segues into a Mind Left Body jam, with Phil Lesh delivering a “phil‑tastic” solo and laying down deep bass bombs in Morning Dew. The encore caps the night with an uplifting Eyes Of The World and a heartfelt Stella Blue, making this performance a standout entry for any 1973 collector. The vault‑remastered soundboard (gd73-10-19.sbd.nayfield.187.sbeok.shnf) captures the full show with clear instrument separation, delivering the most listenable version despite early mix quirks.",
